Compat patch for buffer-equal-constant-time@1.0.1 (transitive dep of jwa) on Node
majors where buffer.SlowBuffer is gone.

Guards index.js:37, `var origSlowBufEqual = SlowBuffer.prototype.equal;`, which reads
SlowBuffer.prototype at load time. Unreachable today: the only consumer, jwa@2.0.1,
requires this module lazily and only when crypto.timingSafeEqual is absent, i.e. on
Node < 6.6. Kept because buffer.SlowBuffer is undefined on Node 26 (still a live
function on Node 24), so the crash goes live at the next Node major bump.

If an upstream change breaks this patch and re-cutting it is costly, deleting it is
defensible provided the reachability above still holds.

Applied by scripts/apply-node-compat-patches.sh.

--- a/node_modules/buffer-equal-constant-time/index.js
+++ b/node_modules/buffer-equal-constant-time/index.js
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
 /*jshint node:true */
 'use strict';
 var Buffer = require('buffer').Buffer; // browserify
-var SlowBuffer = require('buffer').SlowBuffer;
+// Fallback: buffer.SlowBuffer is deprecated (Node 22) and removed in a future major.
+var SlowBuffer = require('buffer').SlowBuffer || function (n) { return Buffer.allocUnsafeSlow(n); };
 
 module.exports = bufferEq;
 
